  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115876",
      "title": "Getting Started with Custom Directives",
      "lectureOrder": 155,
      "videoOrder": 147,
      "sourceHash": "47fa6dc87b0632c6bb3ae057704dc11c897ba7a372e78cb7ee502a18c4dae825",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 2.97,
          "en": "So, now we saw an example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.97,
          "end": 5.43,
          "en": "for a built-in attribute directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.43,
          "end": 9.21,
          "en": "and an example for a built-in structural directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.21,
          "end": 12.24,
          "en": "and I also explained what the differences are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.24,
          "end": 14.97,
          "en": "and what these directives are about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.97,
          "end": 18.51,
          "en": "Now, to get a better understanding of directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.51,
          "end": 21.87,
          "en": "it will definitely help to build a custom directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.87,
          "end": 25.98,
          "en": "and to then use it, and that's therefore what we'll do next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.98,
          "end": 30.453,
          "en": "And I'll start by building a custom structural directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.65,
          "end": 36.65,
          "en": "For that, in the source app folder, anywhere in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.81,
          "end": 40.86,
          "en": "you can add a new file that will hold that directive code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.86,
          "end": 45.3,
          "en": "And here my idea is that I wanna add a directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.3,
          "end": 49.98,
          "en": "that we can add to anchor elements to ask the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.98,
          "end": 52.89,
          "en": "before the link becomes active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.89,
          "end": 55.5,
          "en": "and the user gets navigated away,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.5,
          "end": 58.74,
          "en": "whether they really wanna leave the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.74,
          "end": 62.58,
          "en": "and visit the page the link leads to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.58,
          "end": 66.24,
          "en": "That's a feature you might know from some websites,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.24,
          "end": 70.41,
          "en": "that external links will ask for confirmation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 70.41,
          "end": 73.74,
          "en": "before leading you to that external page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 73.74,
          "end": 76.32,
          "en": "And that's a feature I wanna implement here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.32,
          "end": 78.423,
          "en": "with the help of a custom directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.41,
          "end": 82.89,
          "en": "Therefore, maybe here next to the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.89,
          "end": 87.89,
          "en": "I'll add a new file which I'll name save-link.directive.ts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 89.37,
          "end": 92.943,
          "en": "because I wanna name my directive safe-link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 93.81,
          "end": 96.57,
          "en": "But, of course, as you probably guessed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 96.57,
          "end": 98.07,
          "en": "the name doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.07,
          "end": 100.8,
          "en": "The file, however, should be named like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.8,
          "end": 104.34,
          "en": "since you should still follow that naming convention of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 104.34,
          "end": 106.32,
          "en": "giving things your own name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.32,
          "end": 108.6,
          "en": "that describes what they're about,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.6,
          "end": 112.32,
          "en": "but then also describing the type of Angular feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.32,
          "end": 116.40299999999999,
          "en": "that will be stored in that file, in this case, a directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 117.99000000000001,
          "end": 120.87,
          "en": "Of course, you could also generate directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 120.87,
          "end": 125.16,
          "en": "with ng g directive or ng g d",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 125.16,
          "end": 127.26,
          "en": "with the help of the Angular CLI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 127.26,
          "end": 130.08,
          "en": "but here, to get started, we'll build this directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.08,
          "end": 131.823,
          "en": "from scratch on our own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 132.81,
          "end": 136.07999999999998,
          "en": "So, what does a directive look like then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 136.07999999999998,
          "end": 138.54,
          "en": "Well, it's still a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.54,
          "end": 140.43,
          "en": "a class that should be exported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.43,
          "end": 143.49,
          "en": "to make it available outside of this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.49,
          "end": 145.71,
          "en": "which can have any name you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.71,
          "end": 149.04,
          "en": "but here, in my case, I'll name it SafeLinkDirective",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.04,
          "end": 152.43,
          "en": "and, just as with components, it is the convention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.43,
          "end": 155.28,
          "en": "that you have that \"Directive\" thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.28,
          "end": 157.95,
          "en": "at the end of this class name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.95,
          "end": 160.29,
          "en": "And prior to that, you try to describe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.29,
          "end": 162.543,
          "en": "what this directive will be about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.31,
          "end": 169.31,
          "en": "Now, this class only becomes a directive in Angular's world",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.53,
          "end": 173.88,
          "en": "if you decorate it with the @Directive decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.88,
          "end": 176.793,
          "en": "which must be imported from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 178.05,
          "end": 181.32,
          "en": "So that's important, this decorator must be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 181.32,
          "end": 183.54,
          "en": "just as the @Component decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.54,
          "end": 185.373,
          "en": "must be added to components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 186.36,
          "end": 188.76,
          "en": "And indeed, this directive decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.76,
          "end": 192.21,
          "en": "is quite similar to the component decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.21,
          "end": 194.43,
          "en": "It takes a configuration object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.43,
          "end": 196.59,
          "en": "and there you get some options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.59,
          "end": 198.93,
          "en": "which you also have for components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.93,
          "end": 202.62,
          "en": "like the host option here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.62,
          "end": 204.84,
          "en": "or the selector option,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.84,
          "end": 207.34,
          "en": "which is indeed an option you need to set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 208.26,
          "end": 211.77,
          "en": "because you, of course, need to tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.77,
          "end": 215.25,
          "en": "to which elements this directive should be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.25,
          "end": 219.6,
          "en": "or when this directive should become active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.6,
          "end": 221.91,
          "en": "And you do this with the help of a selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.91,
          "end": 224.82,
          "en": "just as you do it for components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.82,
          "end": 226.77,
          "en": "And just as for components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.77,
          "end": 231.09300000000002,
          "en": "you could set up a tag selector here, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 233.04,
          "end": 235.35,
          "en": "But since the goal of directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 235.35,
          "end": 238.89,
          "en": "in the end is to enhance existing elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 238.89,
          "end": 242.22,
          "en": "you typically don't use the tag selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.22,
          "end": 245.49,
          "en": "or at least not just the tag selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.49,
          "end": 249.69,
          "en": "but instead you typically use the attribute selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 249.69,
          "end": 253.11,
          "en": "so that the directive can be added like an attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 253.11,
          "end": 256.35,
          "en": "onto the element that should be enhanced.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 256.35,
          "end": 259.92,
          "en": "And here we could use appSafeLink, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 259.92,
          "end": 261.42,
          "en": "as an attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 261.42,
          "end": 264.72,
          "en": "It is up to you which attribute you're targeting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.72,
          "end": 268.89,
          "en": "but it should start with a unique prefix like \"app\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 268.89,
          "end": 271.23,
          "en": "to distinguish it from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 271.23,
          "end": 275.043,
          "en": "standard or built-in attributes, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 276.09000000000003,
          "end": 278.73,
          "en": "And you could then combine that, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 278.73,
          "end": 281.55,
          "en": "with the anchor tag selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 281.55,
          "end": 286.29,
          "en": "to apply this directive to any anchor element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 286.29,
          "end": 289.743,
          "en": "that has the appSafeLink attribute on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 290.61,
          "end": 293.07,
          "en": "And that is indeed a selector I'll use here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 293.07,
          "end": 294.75,
          "en": "but in the end it therefore works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 294.75,
          "end": 296.67,
          "en": "just like the component selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 298.95,
          "en": "because you have to select the elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 298.95,
          "end": 303.95,
          "en": "that should be controlled or enhanced by this directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 306.15,
          "end": 308.07,
          "en": "Now, just as with components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 308.07,
          "end": 312.24,
          "en": "you can then also mark directives as standalone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 312.24,
          "end": 315.12,
          "en": "which nowadays is the recommended approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 315.12,
          "end": 318.513,
          "en": "so this should be set to true nowadays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 319.47,
          "end": 322.68,
          "en": "In older Angular versions this would be false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 322.68,
          "end": 326.52,
          "en": "or this setting wouldn't exist at all, to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 326.52,
          "end": 328.77,
          "en": "But nowadays it should be set to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 328.77,
          "end": 332.88,
          "en": "so that you can use this directive without NgModules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 332.88,
          "end": 336.99,
          "en": "just as you can use components without NgModules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 336.99,
          "end": 339.93,
          "en": "as you saw in this course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 339.93,
          "end": 342.54,
          "en": "Well, and that's then the bare minimum",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 342.54,
          "end": 345.39300000000003,
          "en": "configuration you need for a directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 346.65,
          "end": 349.02,
          "en": "Now, here I'll add a constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 349.02,
          "end": 351.157,
          "en": "where I'll simply console.log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 351.157,
          "end": 355.227,
          "en": "\"SafeLink directive is active\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 356.19,
          "end": 359.07,
          "en": "to get some feedback whether this directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 359.07,
          "end": 362.46,
          "en": "is having an effect or is being loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 362.46,
          "end": 364.653,
          "en": "and applied to an element or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 366.81,
          "end": 368.94,
          "en": "And therefore now with that all added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 368.94,
          "end": 373.41,
          "en": "we can and should go to the place where we want to use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 373.41,
          "end": 376.263,
          "en": "in my case, the learning resources template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 377.76,
          "end": 381.42,
          "en": "And there, on that first link, I'll add this directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 381.42,
          "end": 386.42,
          "en": "by adding the appSafeLink attribute, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 387.3,
          "end": 388.71,
          "en": "And, of course, it must be written",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 388.71,
          "end": 391.47,
          "en": "just the way it is written here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 391.47,
          "end": 392.90999999999997,
          "en": "without the square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 392.90999999999997,
          "end": 396.27,
          "en": "since that's just the CSS selector syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 396.27,
          "end": 398.313,
          "en": "for selecting an attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 399.15,
          "end": 403.02,
          "en": "The attribute name is the part between the square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 403.02,
          "end": 405.3,
          "en": "Now, here I'm selecting all anchor elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 405.3,
          "end": 407.31,
          "en": "that have this attribute on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 407.31,
          "end": 409.5,
          "en": "and since I have an anchor element here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 409.5,
          "end": 411.09000000000003,
          "en": "with that attribute on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 411.09000000000003,
          "end": 414.453,
          "en": "the directive should be active for that element here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 415.38,
          "end": 419.61,
          "en": "And with that, if we go back and open the developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 419.61,
          "end": 421.83,
          "en": "and there the console;",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 421.83,
          "end": 425.283,
          "en": "if I reload nothing's happening.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 426.18,
          "end": 428.46,
          "en": "Well, and nothing's happening here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 428.46,
          "end": 431.67,
          "en": "because, of course, Angular doesn't really know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 431.67,
          "end": 435.63,
          "en": "this directive yet, or doesn't see that this attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 435.63,
          "end": 438.84,
          "en": "on this element should attach some directive here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 438.84,
          "end": 443.22,
